#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/ansible.rst:164
msgid ""
"Another great feature with using Ansible and |morpheus| together is the "
"built in support for utilizing some of the services that |morpheus| "
"exposes for automation. One of these great services is known as Cypher "
"(please see documentation on :ref:`Cypher` for more details). Cypher "
"allows one to store secret data in a highly encrypted way for future "
"retrieval. Referencing keys stored in cypher in your playbooks is a "
"matter of using a built-in lookup plugin for ansible."
msgstr "QueuePolicy"

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/ansible.rst:166
msgid ""
"- name: Add a user\n"
"  win_user:\n"
"    name: \"myusername\"\n"
"    password: \"{{ lookup('cypher','secret=password/myusername') }}\"\n"
"    state: present"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/ansible.rst:175
msgid ""
"By using the ``{{ lookup('cypher','secret=password/myusername') }}`` "
"syntax. One can grab the value directly out of the key for use. This "
"lookup plugin also supports a few other fancy shortcuts. In this above "
"example the `password/` mountpoint is capable of autogenerating passwords"
" if they have not previously been defined and storing them within cypher "
"for reference later."
msgstr "En utilisant la syntaxe ``{{ lookup('cypher','secret=password/myusername') }}``. On peut récupérer la valeur directement depuis la clé. Ce plug-in de recherche prend également en charge quelques autres raccourcis. Dans l'exemple ci-dessus, le point de montage `password/` est capable de générer automatiquement des mots de passe s'ils n'ont pas été définis auparavant et de les stocker dans cypher pour référence ultérieure."

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/ansible.rst:177
msgid ""
"Another capability is accessing properties from within a key in cypher. "
"The value of a key can also be a JSON object which can be referenced for "
"properties within. For example:"
msgstr "ByteMatchSet"

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/ansible.rst:179
msgid "{{ lookup('cypher','secret=secret/myjsonobject:value') }}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/ansible.rst:183
msgid ""
"This would grab the `value` property off the nested json data stored "
"within the key."
msgstr "IPSet"

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/ansible.rst:185
msgid ""
"Cypher is very powerful for storing these temporary or permanent secrets "
"that one may need to orchestrate various tasks and workflows within "
"Ansible."
msgstr "Ensemble de correspondance d'octets AWS WAF Regional"

